XC.newzealand={cc:'NZ',first:['Aroha','Tane','Hemi','Mere','Rawiri','Kiri','Wiremu','Anahera','Manu','Huia','Tama','Ngaio','Hine','Rangi','Maia','Kahu'],last:['Te Rangi','Parata','Tamihana','Walker','Ngata','Hohepa','Kereama','Wiremu','Tuhiwai','Rewi','Paewai','Hapi','Mahuta','Pere','Karaka','Waititi'],facts:['insists a hangi dinner is worth waiting hours for, because the earth oven never rushes','can do the hongi greeting so warmly that you feel like family within one breath','will tell you Aotearoa means land of the long white cloud and then point at the actual cloud','can explain why a haka is about pride and unity, not just stomping and looking fierce'],fig:{'Maui':['Legendary trickster who fished the North Island up from the sea with a magic hook','Slowed the sun with a rope so the day would be long enough to get things done'],'Kupe':['Legendary Polynesian navigator credited with first reaching Aotearoa','Is said to have chased a giant octopus across the ocean, which is quite a commute'],'Hone Heke':['Ngapuhi chief who famously cut down the British flagpole at Kororareka more than once','Proved that persistence is a great hobby'],'Dame Whina Cooper':['Led the 1975 Maori Land March from the far north to Wellington at age 79','Showed that a long walk can be a very loud argument']}};
XC.samoa={cc:'WS',first:['Tui','Sina','Lua','Fa’amoe','Malia','Tevita','Losa','Iosefa','Alofa','Manu','Leilani','Sione','Tala','Moana','Faith','Pele'],last:['Tuala','Faleolo','Leota','Aiono','Sapolu','Fuimaono','Toleafoa','Lealaiauloto','Malietoa','Soifua','Tuiasosopo','Afamasaga','Schmidt','Salevao','Seiuli','Vaai'],facts:['insists the best fale has no walls, because the breeze is already the air conditioner','can sit through a long fa’alavelave gathering and still bring snacks home for everyone','will explain that a fine mat is worth more than most things money can buy','can cook a whole umu feast and keep the family arguing happily about who is in charge'],fig:{'Nafanua':['War goddess of Samoa who, legend says, rose from the earth to defend her people','Is remembered as the one who united the islands under peaceful rule'],'Sina':['Heroine of many Samoan legends, including the tale of the eel that became the first coconut','Proof that sometimes love stories end with a snack'],'Robert Louis Stevenson':['Scottish author who settled in Samoa and was called Tusitala, teller of tales','Was so loved that villagers cut a road to his house and named it the Road of the Loving Heart'],'Tupua Tamasese Lealofi III':['Leader of the Mau movement who worked peacefully for Samoan self-rule','Helped lay the path to independence in 1962, the first in Polynesia']}};
XC.tonga={cc:'TO',first:['Sione','Mele','Siaosi','Seini','Tevita','Losaline','Viliami','Ofa','Saia','Lupe','Pita','Sela','Mosese','Ana','Kalolaine','Fifita'],last:['Tupou','Fifita','Havili','Latu','Fonua','Vaipulu','Taufa','Kioa','Tuku’aho','Lavulavu','Moala','Vea','Funaki','Maka','Pulu','Halafihi'],facts:['insists Tonga is the Friendly Islands and will prove it by feeding you twice before you sit down','can tell you with pride that Tonga was never colonised','will wake up early for a church choir whose harmonies could rattle a whole village','can say Tonga is where the new day starts, so tomorrow arrives here first'],fig:{'Queen Salote Tupou III':['Reigned for nearly 50 years and was beloved at home and abroad','Won hearts at the 1953 coronation in London by riding in the rain with her carriage hood down'],'King Taufa’ahau Tupou I':['United the islands and created the Tongan kingdom in the 1800s','Gave Tonga one of the first written constitutions in the Pacific'],'Maui':['Legendary figure said in Tongan lore to have fished islands up from the sea','His hook is still blamed whenever land seems oddly shaped'],'Jonah Lomu':['Tongan-descended rugby star who became a global sensation at the 1995 World Cup','Was so fast for his size that defenders reportedly just hoped for the best']}};
XC.hawaii={cc:'US',first:['Kekoa','Leilani','Keanu','Malia','Kai','Noelani','Makoa','Kalani','Lani','Koa','Haunani','Nalu','Mahina','Keala','Pua','Kainoa'],last:['Kamakana','Kealoha','Akana','Nakamura','Kahale','Kamaka','Kapule','Keawe','Kekumu','Silva','Medeiros','Kaneshiro','Pau','Mahoe','Kalama','Souza'],facts:['insists you take your slippers off at the door, and honestly you should','can tell you a good plate lunch needs two scoops of rice and zero apologies','will say aloha means far more than hello and goodbye, and is correct','can calmly explain that the mountain with the best sunrise is also a volcano'],fig:{'Pele':['Goddess of volcanoes and fire, said to live in Kilauea','Is believed to be quite particular about which rocks leave her island'],'Duke Kahanamoku':['Olympic swimming champion who helped spread surfing around the world','Once used his surfboard to rescue several people from a capsized boat in 1925'],'Queen Liliuokalani':['Last reigning monarch of the Hawaiian Kingdom and a gifted songwriter','Wrote Aloha Oe, one of the best loved songs in the islands'],'Maui':['Demigod who lassoed the sun on Haleakala to lengthen the day','Also tricked fire out of mud hens, so he is a hero for the barbecue crowd']}};
XC.tahiti={cc:'PF',first:['Teiva','Moana','Heiata','Tehei','Vaiana','Manua','Hinano','Tiare','Teva','Maeva','Tamatoa','Poema','Rava','Mareva','Tauhiti','Vaea'],last:['Tetuanui','Teriierooiterai','Tehaamoana','Pomare','Tauira','Temaiana','Teuira','Taputu','Tevane','Tuheiava','Maraeura','Teihotu','Hiro','Atger','Rohfritsch','Salmon'],facts:['insists a morning baguette from the roulotte is as much an island tradition as the ukulele','can wear a flower crown so naturally that it looks like part of the hairstyle','will tell you the tiare Tahiti is the national flower and you will be handed one before you can answer','can dance the tamure so fast that people ask whether the hips are on a motor'],fig:{'Hiro':['Legendary navigator and god of Raiatea, patron of thieves and voyagers','Is said to have raised sacred canoes that sailed the whole Pacific'],'Queen Pomare IV':['Ruled Tahiti for 50 years and defended her kingdom against foreign powers','Stood her ground through some very complicated diplomacy'],'Tafai':['Said in legend to be the demigod who gave the island its shape','Is credited with fishing parts of the land out of the sea'],'Paul Gauguin':['French painter who lived in Tahiti and painted its people and colours','Is buried in the Marquesas, and his art made the islands famous worldwide']}};
XC.cookislands={cc:'CK',first:['Tamati','Teina','Mere','Ngaire','Tere','Rangi','Mata','Tuaine','Ana','Teuira','Maara','Taia','Tiare','Pa','Moana','Nooroa'],last:['Henry','Puna','Tamarua','Browne','Marsters','Piri','Tangaroa','Ngatamariki','Mataio','Kauvai','Rakanui','Ioane','Taripo','Pokino','Napa','Tauei'],facts:['insists a coconut is a drink, a bowl and a hat if you are patient enough','can say there are only about fifteen islands but each one has its own opinion','will tell you the Cook Islands are in free association with New Zealand and mostly want to talk about fish','can drum along at a Te Maeva Nui celebration without looking at a score'],fig:{'Tangiia':['Legendary navigator who settled Rarotonga','Is said to have brought breadfruit and traditions with him from Tahiti'],'Io':['Supreme being in some Polynesian traditions and the island lore of the Cooks','Is reputed to have created the world by saying it out loud'],'Dr Tom Davis':['Pacific physician and Prime Minister who sailed the ocean in a yacht','Wrote books about his voyages and made a doctor look very adventurous'],'Queen Makea Takau':['Ariki of the Takitumu people who signed the 1888 request for British protection','Led her people with great dignity through a time of big change']}};
XC.tuvalu={cc:'TV',first:['Kaitu','Sina','Teuila','Tavita','Selu','Melina','Falealili','Lagi','Mati','Penitala','Ioane','Alapati','Tauasa','Fakaofo','Nei','Taupule'],last:['Teo','Sopoaga','Telavi','Kofe','Lauti','Italeli','Puapua','Natano','Panapa','Tuilaepa','Seluka','Maatia','Tafia','Afele','Pelesala','Kilei'],facts:['insists Tuvalu is small but the hospitality is enormous','can tell you the country has a famous internet domain, .tv, and enjoys the joke','will point out that fatele dances start with everyone in a circle and end with everyone laughing','can fish from a canoe and chat about weather in the same breath'],fig:{'Tefolaha':['Legendary ancestor who is said to have arrived by canoe and settled Nanumea','Is remembered in many family stories across the atolls'],'Ionatana Ionatana':['Early Tuvaluan leader who served as Prime Minister','Is remembered as a calm voice in the country early independent years'],'Toaripi Lauti':['First Prime Minister of Tuvalu after independence in 1978','Helped guide the islands to become their own nation'],'Hatesa':['Mythical hero in Tuvaluan lore of Nui','Said to be a clever wanderer, like a good storyteller']}};
XC.niue={cc:'NU',first:['Tui','Mele','Sione','Lagi','Moana','Fiafia','Ana','Pita','Tangi','Liku','Tala','Lupe','Kalani','Falala','Hiva','Mata'],last:['Talagi','Tagaloa','Lui','Pavihi','Tongatule','Tuhipa','Hekesi','Funaki','Magatogia','Sionetuato','Tukuitonga','Liuvaie','Vilitama','Mokalei','Kulatea','Pulu'],facts:['insists Niue is the Rock of Polynesia and one of the biggest raised coral islands anywhere','can swim in a sea chasm so clear that you wonder where the water went','will tell you the island has some of the clearest ocean visibility on Earth and then ask if you want to swim','can explain, with no hurry, why the sea tracks are worth the climb down'],fig:{'Fao':['Legendary hero said in Niuean tradition to have helped shape the island','Is remembered in stories of the first settlers'],'Tui Tonga Fafine':['Legendary female figure tied to Tongan and Niuean ancestry','Is linked in tradition to the origins of Polynesian chiefly lines'],'Sir Robert Rex':['First Resident Commissioner and later Niue first Premier-era leader recognised by Niueans','Is remembered for guiding the island through a difficult period'],'Hiapo makers':['Women of Niue who painted bark cloth called hiapo with bold patterns','Their art can be found in museums, which is a fine end for tapa']}};
XC.tokelau={cc:'TK',first:['Tuhaepa','Mele','Sina','Pio','Fetu','Toloa','Lagi','Aliki','Teuila','Tomasi','Fakaofo','Ioane','Mase','Tala','Hina','Lupe'],last:['Kalolo','Perez','Tuhipa','Faleolo','Lui','Pasilio','Falaniko','Elisala','Tuia','Iupati','Napa','Aukuso','Toloa','Nasau','Pelasio','Tialeni'],facts:['insists three little atolls can be a whole nation with plenty of heart','can paddle a canoe across a lagoon while singing at full volume','will say that with no airport the ship from Samoa is the highlight of the week','can explain how a village runs by taking turns, and everyone agrees surprisingly quickly'],fig:{'Tui Tokelau':['Tokelau is said to have had a mythical chief by that title in tradition','Is mentioned in stories about the first canoe landings'],'Tinirau':['Legendary Polynesian figure of the sea, famed for his pet whale','Is said to have kept fish and sea creatures the way most of us keep cats'],'Maui':['Demigod whose hook is part of lore across the Pacific, Tokelau included','Pulled up islands and then asked for no credit'],'Kolouei O Tokelau':['Local leader recognised for his guidance during modern times','Is remembered with good humour at community gatherings']}};
XC.americansamoa={cc:'AS',first:['Tui','Sina','Junior','Malia','Faafetai','Lupe','Mikaele','Tala','Losa','Siaosi','Fia','Sione','Mele','Aleki','Leilani','Manu'],last:['Faleomavaega','Lutu','Tuiasosopo','Fuimaono','Peko','Moliga','Tuitele','Sunia','Salave’a','Pulu','Te’o','Soliai','Toala','Lealao','Seumalo','Fiaui'],facts:['insists American Samoa has the best of two worlds, island time and Friday night football','can tell you the NFL has an amazing number of Samoan players for such a small place','will point out that Pago Pago harbor is one of the deepest and most sheltered in the Pacific','can cook an umu feast and also cheer for a high school game with equal passion'],fig:{'Faleomavaega Eni Hunkin':['Represented American Samoa in the US Congress for many years','Was known for speaking up for the Pacific islands in Washington'],'Troy Polamalu':['American football star of Samoan heritage with a world-famous head of hair','Won two Super Bowls with the Steelers, and his hair got its own commercials'],'Nafanua':['War goddess whose story is shared across Samoa','Is said to have ended wars and welcomed peace'],'Tauese Sunia':['Governor of American Samoa who served in the late 1990s and early 2000s','Is remembered as a steady, gentle leader']}};
XC.rapanui={cc:'CL',first:['Hotu','Tiare','Anakena','Moana','Rano','Poike','Tangata','Haumaka','Matari','Koro','Nua','Vaitea','Hina','Ure','Maunga','Tuhi'],last:['Pakarati','Hito','Tuki','Teao','Paoa','Haoa','Pate','Tepano','Atan','Tuki','Rapu','Chavez','Icka','Hey','Edmunds','Riroroko'],facts:['insists the moai were not just statues, they were ancestors who kept watch','can say there is no place on Earth as far from anywhere as Rapa Nui, and mean it fondly','will tell you the island is also called Te Pito o Te Henua, the navel of the world','can sing at a Tapati festival and make a canoe race seem as important as the Olympics'],fig:{'Hotu Matua':['Legendary first king who is said to have led settlers to Rapa Nui by canoe','Brought plants and traditions across the sea, which is a very long way to bring a garden'],'Make Make':['Creator god of the Rapa Nui people and the center of the birdman cult','Is shown in carvings as a face with big watchful eyes'],'Tangata manu':['The Birdman, chosen each year by a daring swim and race to Motu Nui','Won by fetching the first sooty tern egg, no matter how tricky the cliff'],'Ariki Mau':['Title of the paramount chief of Rapa Nui','Is remembered as a keeper of the island tradition']}};
XC.wallisfutuna={cc:'WF',first:['Sione','Malia','Petelo','Mele','Soane','Lusia','Felise','Atonio','Sina','Tomasi','Seini','Lavinia','Pelenato','Savelina','Manuele','Lupe'],last:['Tuiasosopo','Takaniko','Lutui','Faupala','Tuiagaifo','Tautuku','Fenuafanote','Tukumuli','Manuopuava','Vaitootai','Hoatau','Lavelua','Takala','Kulimoetoke','Lakina','Halagahu'],facts:['insists that Wallis and Futuna is a French territory where the kava ceremony still matters more than the clock','can explain how three traditional kingdoms share two small islands with calm good humour','will say that a pig at a feast is a sign of real respect','can speak Wallisian, Futunan and French and switch with the weather'],fig:{'Pierre Chanel':['French missionary who was killed on Futuna in 1841 and later became a saint','Is still remembered each April on the island'],'Lavelua':['Title of the traditional king of Uvea on Wallis','Has been held by a long line of rulers who keep the old customs alive'],'Tuiagaifo':['Title of the king of Sigave on Futuna, one of the traditional kingdoms','Still holds a role in island ceremonies'],'Tu’i Tonga':['Tongan ruler whose influence reached many parts of Polynesia, Wallis included','Is said to have left words and customs that still echo there']}};
